description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, carry the parent's failure lessons into a narrowed gap so the child is more informative than its parent.

ANCHOR. This exact line occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file:
        const childMeta = { ...meta, failed_attempts: 0, parent_gap_id: parentId, narrowed_at: new Date().toISOString() };

ONE OPERATION. Insert the following three lines IMMEDIATELY AFTER that line, at the same indentation:

        const priorLessons = Array.isArray((meta as Record<string, unknown>)["failure_lessons"]) ? ((meta as Record<string, unknown>)["failure_lessons"] as Array<Record<string, unknown>>) : [];
        const lessonList = priorLessons.slice(-3).map((l) => "- " + String(l["class"] ?? "?") + ": " + String(l["reason"] ?? "").slice(0, 300)).join("\n");
        const lessonBlock = lessonList.length === 0 ? "" : "\n\nWHY PREVIOUS ATTEMPTS ON THIS GAP FAILED (carried forward, most recent last):\n" + lessonList + "\n\nDo not repeat these failures. Address the specific cause named above.";

Use plain string concatenation exactly as written above. Do NOT use template literals or backticks anywhere in the inserted lines. Change nothing else in this operation.

WHY. This is the chronic-failure narrowing branch. It fires when a gap has already failed repeatedly, and the comment above it states "The child carries a tighter description" — but the child summary is currently the parent's text with a prefix prepended, so a fresh attempt receives exactly the description that already failed at least three times. The failure lessons are already attached to the gap in classification_metadata.failure_lessons, holding the class and reason for each prior attempt, and `meta` is in scope here because it is spread into childMeta on the anchor line itself. This computes the block; a follow-up change will append it to the summary.

MEASURED JUSTIFICATION. Paired within-gap comparison over 259 parent/narrowed pairs: landing 7.3% (19/259) for parents versus 7.7% (20/259) for their narrowed children, and the share of summaries carrying a concrete proposed change rises only from 5% to 8%. 259 narrowing operations for a 0.4 percentage-point difference, because the description carried across is unchanged.

SAFETY. These three lines only declare local constants and have no effect on behaviour by themselves — nothing reads lessonBlock yet, so this change cannot alter what the substrate does. It is deliberately inert on its own so it can be verified before anything consumes it. When there are no prior lessons, lessonBlock is the empty string.

